== fm-spend-profile
ok - a dispatch file without spend_profiles launches and records exactly as before
ok - a CAPPZ project resolves to the personal store and a Spire project to the work store
ok - a CAPPZ task asking for Opus or Sonnet on the personal profile is refused before launch
ok - a pi-account that disagrees with the project's profile is refused in both directions
ok - a project that is not in the profile map refuses to launch, ship or scout, until it is mapped
ok - a profile other than the project's own needs the captain's words, and the record keeps them
ok - a harness that cannot pin the profile's account, and a raw Pi command, are refused
ok - malformed spend profiles, a shared store, and an unreadable spend-profile file refuse before launch
ok - a secondmate spawn is exempt from project profiles and refuses --profile
ok - the day-one example maps work, personal, and unmapped projects as today's routing requires
# all fm-spend-profile tests passed
== fm-dispatch-resolve
ok - declared provider and profile floor evidence are applied in code
ok - nonnumeric spendPriority evidence is never ranked
ok - partial and missing quota evidence remain eligible but unranked
ok - provider-wide and exact quota rows combine into one limiting candidate
ok - default: no rule matched resolves among the default profiles
ok - tie: equal spendPriority never breaks by array order
ok - no rankable candidate: the tool escalates instead of guessing
ok - native Codex binds to codex-home before default, independently of Pi accounts and row order
ok - Pi native adapters bind to codex-home with existing fallbacks and schema 5 compatibility
ok - schema 6: each candidate binds to its account row; schema 5 is unchanged
ok - quota evidence comes from one quota-axi --json read, and its failure is an error outcome
ok - API, transport, and response failures are error outcomes with exit 0
ok - configuration errors exit 2 before any network call
ok - under spend profiles the resolver request carries only the project's profile rules, built offline
# all fm-dispatch-resolve tests passed
